rd Khal Drogo  he'd already earned more than enough bad  guy points to deserve death by molten  metal crown fit for king sized tool of  course Viserys isn't the only person in  Game of Thrones with a death wish  Joffrey Baratheon Game of Thrones in a  way it's hard to blame Joffrey Baratheon  for being such a sniveling little creep  after all he was the product of  inbreeding and growing up in a royal  court man he was constant  spoiled still that doesn't excuse his  bloodthirsty rule as king or his  violence against women committed to  getting his own way at all costs  Joffrey proved a consistent irritant  during Game of Thrones first four  seasons so it came as a delightful  relief when he was poisoned by his own  grandmother in law at his wedding of all  the many many deaths Game of Thrones has  given viewers Joffrey's extermination  has to be the most satisfying Robert  Romano er unlike most of the characters  on this list er's Robert Romano wasn't a  killer or even a criminal he was just a  token smug doctor that every hospital  show has to have it's the actor palma  cranes credit that Romano ends up being  such as satisfying love to hate him  thorne in the staff side after being  introduced in the show's fourth season  he manages to offend alienate and insult  just about every other character all  while adding to the top-rated shows  consistently riveting drama Romano goes  out the bang in season 10 paying for his  TV sins by being crushed under a  helicopter that falls off the hospital  roof at that point we were more worried  about the helicopter Phillip Blake the  walking dead like any good sociopath The  Walking Dead's governor Phillip Blake is  a smooth enough talker to keep his true  nature hidden from his friends and  allies for a short time at least during  the show's third and fourth seasons  Blake's bloodlust and thirst for power  revealed in small increments by the time  we figure out he's a murderous lunatic  who keeps his zombified daughter  restrained in his apartment we're pretty  much counting down the days until his  death even for the Walking Dead the  governor's demise is pretty gruesome but  a viewer has ever wanted to see someone  get stabbed in the back shot in the head  and left in a field to be dismembered it  was all one eye speaking of putting your  eye out Gustavo Fring Breaking Bad if  you start selling meth for a living  you're bound to run into some pretty  unsavory characters case in point  Gus fring the powerful lethal dealer who  starts tightening a noose around Walter  White's neck almost immediately after he  reaches out to him about distributing  his perfect product throughout the  show's third and fourth seasons Gus and  Walter fight each other for the upper  hand in the relationship with enough  twists turns and double crosses for an  entire series we felt a powerful rush a  satisfaction when Walter finally got rid  of Gus by booby trapping an enemy's  wheelchair with a bomb that took off  half of Gus's face and a small chunk of  a nursing home  real nice well Arthur Mitchell Dexter  John Lithgow went from playing third  rocked and the Sons doofy sitcom dad to  giving us the creeps as Arthur Mitchell  the spine-tingling serial murderer known  as the Trinity Killer in the fourth  season of Dexter Lithgow soft-spoken  Demeter made him the perfect choice to  play a guy who's near perfect suburban  existence masks a terrifying urge to  kill this help fill an entire season  with a steadily mounting sense of dread  that still lingered even after Dexter  manages to finally put an end Michels  murderous ways in a sickening twist the  show undercut the viewers relief over  the Trinity killers death by revealing  that Dexter caught Mitchell too late to  prevent him from committing his last  murder  Dexter's own wife Rita Ralph Cifaretto  The Sopranos a career criminal whose  tendency toward violent outbursts was  overlooked because of his ability to get  things done Ralphie was a longtime Burr